# These run on Linux, from systemd and from root shells. A CRLF in a shell script
# fails as `syntax error near unexpected token $'do\r'` -- and only once a `for` or
# `while` lands in it, so it can ride along invisibly for a long time first.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
